{"pageid": 900, "title": "Scarlet Mask", "revid": 2782, "categories": ["Lore", "Masks", "Monster hunters", "Order of St. George", "Scarlet Masks"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/f/f3/Scarlet_Mask.png/revision/latest?cb=20241130215725\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"The Scarlet Mask of the North American Houses.\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/f/f3/Scarlet_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241130215725\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"98\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Scarlet Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"Scarlet_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Scarlet_Mask.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">The Scarlet Mask of the North American Houses.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<p><b>Scarlet Masks</b> are a branch of <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a> who don the color red and serve as book- and housekeepers of their specified House. Extremely important to the Order as their record-keepers, they are also sometimes looked down upon by Hunters as simply servants. However, they help all Houses run smoothly, keep track of every Hunter, and catalog information for future reference.\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>Scarlet Masks are the keepers of their House and its records. They make sure the House is kept in pristine condition, feeding its hunters, washing their clothes, cleaning their rooms. They also oversee the library of each House, recording each hunter's missions, and documenting the different classes of monsters the hunters face in their work, so that the House can learn from its past mistakes and rise above them into the future. They write in the blood of monsters so that only members of the Order can read their work. The majority of those who decide not to participate in the Blind Hunt become Scarlet Masks.</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Slaughter_1\" title=\"Book of Slaughter 1\">The Book of Slaughter</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The Scarlet Masks are not active hunters within the Order of St. George. While initially trained as White or Black Masks, many apprentices either feel their calling within the record-keeping or housekeeping aspects of the Scarlet life, or else find themselves unlikely to survive <span class=\"new\" title=\"The Sacrament of Trepanation (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGhlX1NhY3JhbWVudF9vZl9UcmVwYW5hdGlvbj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">the Blind Hunt</span> and wish for some other way to be useful without field work. There are multiple Scarlet Masks within each House, in order to keep it all in proper order so that the Hunters don't have to worry about their base of operations. \n</p><p>The main job of the Scarlets is to catalog information within the Order. They will record every hunter's missions, life, and death; as well as every monster sighting, behavior pattern, and death. They oversee the library, usually keeping books written only in monster-blood so only those of the Order can read their contents.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOS&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOS-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> In short, the members of this branch are usually organizational, ordered, and perceptive.\n</p><p>Often, Hunters look down upon Scarlet Masks as unskilled laborers; this isn't helped by the fact the Scarlets also take care of each House, and thus act as mealmakers and cleaners for the other Masks, which give them the perception of servants.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOS&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOS-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> This can also cause Scarlets to consider other Masks to be rude, thoughtless, and stupid.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS28&#95;2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS28-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> The Scarlets are not to be underestimated, however, as they hold knowledge of every aspect of the House, a large amount of the Order's history, and secrets many other Masks will never be privy to.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS27&#95;3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS27-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Known_Scarlet_Masks\">Known Scarlet Masks</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"House_of_Boucher\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"La Maison de Boucher (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTGFfTWFpc29uX2RlX0JvdWNoZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">House of Boucher</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Tobias Boucher (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVG9iaWFzX0JvdWNoZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Tobias Boucher</span></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"House_of_Carnage\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"House of Carnage (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSG91c2Vfb2ZfQ2FybmFnZT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">House of Carnage</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"François Carnage (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRnJhbiVDMyVBN29pc19DYXJuYWdlP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">François Carnage</span> † (d. 8/14/1666)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"House_of_Cutter\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"House of Cutter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSG91c2Vfb2ZfQ3V0dGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">House of Cutter</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Samuel_Slaughter\" title=\"Samuel Slaughter\">Samuel Cutter</a> † <small>(defected, later founded the House of Slaughter as a <a href=\"/wiki/Black_Mask\" title=\"Black Mask\">Black Mask</a>)</small></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Albie_Cutter\" title=\"Albie Cutter\">Albie Cutter</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"House_of_Slaughter\"><a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Slaughter\" title=\"House of Slaughter\">House of Slaughter</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Colin Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQ29saW5fU2xhdWdodGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Colin Slaughter</span><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS30&#95;4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS30-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> <small>(head)</small></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Gerde Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR2VyZGVfU2xhdWdodGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Gerde Slaughter</span> † (d. 2021)</li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Edwin Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRWR3aW5fU2xhdWdodGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Edwin Slaughter</span> <small>(transferred tp <a href=\"/wiki/Silver_Mask\" title=\"Silver Mask\">Silver Mask</a>)</small></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"6102268e04dc152a347e31e887c33c9c\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:187px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Scarlet_Mask-png\" style=\"position: relative; height:100px; width:185px; top:42.5px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Scarlet_Mask.png\" title=\"Scarlet Mask.png (583 KB)\" style=\"height:100px; width:185px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/f/f3/Scarlet_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/185?cb=20241130215725\" title=\"Scarlet Mask.png (583 KB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"The Scarlet Mask of the American Houses.\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Scarlet Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"Scarlet_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-caption=\"The Scarlet Mask of the American Houses.\"></noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" title=\"Scarlet Mask.png (583 KB)\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" alt=\"The Scarlet Mask of the American Houses.\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Scarlet Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"Scarlet_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-caption=\"The Scarlet Mask of the American Houses.\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/f/f3/Scarlet_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/185?cb=2024113021